node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
# Incremental-build state from the host.
#
# `**/dist` keeps compiled output out of the build context, but the matching
# `*.tsbuildinfo` was still copied in. tsc then read a manifest saying every
# file was already emitted, emitted nothing, and exited 0 — so the image built
# from a workspace with no `dist` at all and the API compile failed with 1323
# "cannot find module '@palcert/contracts'" errors. A build must not depend on
# whether somebody ran a typecheck on the machine that started it.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.next
**/coverage
**/generated
.git
.github
docs
test-documents
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
